<%@ page contentType="text/html;charset=UTF-8" pageEncoding="UTF-8" %>
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Network Topology · TorchNode</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/topology.css"></head><body><%@ include file="layout.jsp" %>
<main class="shell" id="topology-app"><header><p class="eyebrow">OBSERVED EVIDENCE / PHASE B5</p><h1>Network Topology Intelligence</h1><p>Recorded cryptographic identities and attributable relationships from this observer. This is not a map of Ethereum peer connectivity.</p></header>
<section class="notice" aria-labelledby="topology-limits"><h2 id="topology-limits">Directed discovery reports with immutable evidence</h2><p>Arrows mean an authenticated responder reported the target ENR. They do not establish TCP, RLPx or ETH sessions, bidirectional communication, global adjacency or geographic proximity. Legacy identities remain unlinked.</p><p>Degree, components, repeated relationships and relationship freshness remain unavailable. Node spacing below is arbitrary and conveys no physical distance or connectivity.</p></section>
<form id="topology-filters" class="panel controls"><label>Quick window<select id="topology-range"><option value="1">24 hours</option><option value="7">7 days</option><option value="30">30 days</option></select></label><label>Current start UTC<input type="datetime-local" id="topology-start" step="1" required></label><label>Current end UTC<input type="datetime-local" id="topology-end" step="1" required></label><label>Discovery protocol<select id="topology-protocol"><option value="all">All evidence domains</option><option value="discv4">discv4 receipts</option><option value="discv5">discv5 receipts</option></select></label><label>Relationship filter<select id="topology-relation"><option value="all">All supported types</option><option>DISCOVERED_BY</option><option>REPORTED_NEIGHBOR</option><option>DIRECT_SESSION</option></select></label><label>Evidence availability<select id="topology-availability"><option value="all">All stored identity and relationship evidence</option><option value="attributable">Attributable relationships</option><option value="identity-only">Legacy identity evidence</option></select></label><label>Observer installation UUID<input id="topology-observer" maxlength="36"></label><label>Identity hex prefix<input id="topology-search" type="search" maxlength="128" pattern="[a-fA-F0-9]*" placeholder="Public key prefix; not an IP"></label><label>Graph page size<select id="topology-limit"><option>50</option><option selected>100</option><option>200</option></select></label><button id="topology-load" type="submit">Measure window</button></form>
<p id="topology-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading recorded identities…</p><button id="topology-retry" type="button" hidden>Retry graph request</button><a id="topology-login" href="/login" hidden>Sign in again</a>
<div id="topology-kpis" class="kpis"></div>
<div class="topology-grid"><section class="panel graph-panel"><div class="graph-toolbar"><h2>Observed identity graph</h2><% if(Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getAttribute("isAdmin"))){ %><a id="topology-export" hidden href="/api/v1/topology/exports/graph.json">Export evidence page JSON</a><% } %><button id="topology-print" type="button" disabled>Print evidence report</button><button id="topology-zoom-in" type="button" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button><button id="topology-zoom-out" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button><button id="topology-reset" type="button">Reset / fit to view</button><button id="topology-next" type="button" hidden>Next identity page</button></div><p id="topology-caption">At most 200 identities. Drag to pan; use zoom controls, wheel, +/− or arrow keys. Select a point or a row below.</p><svg id="topology-graph" viewBox="0 0 960 620" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Bounded graph of recorded identities with no inferred connectivity" aria-describedby="topology-caption"><g id="topology-viewport"></g></svg><p id="topology-empty" hidden>No timestamped identity evidence matches this scope.</p><div class="legend"><span>● Recorded identity claim</span><span>● Validated ENR identity</span><span>Arrows: authenticated REPORTED_NEIGHBOR · no isolation inference</span></div><details><summary>Relationship semantics</summary><ul><li>DISCOVERED_BY: discovered identity → observer.</li><li>REPORTED_NEIGHBOR: responder → returned identity. An advertisement is not a peer session.</li><li>DIRECT_SESSION: actual local session identity → authenticated remote identity at a recorded clock.</li></ul><p>Only attributable REPORTED_NEIGHBOR evidence is rendered. Missing edges do not mean disconnected nodes.</p></details></section>
<aside class="panel"><h2>Selection & source evidence</h2><div id="topology-selection" aria-live="polite">Select an identity to inspect its records.</div><button id="topology-neighborhood" type="button" hidden>Load observed neighborhood</button><p id="topology-neighborhood-status" role="status"></p><div id="topology-evidence"></div></aside></div>
<details class="panel"><summary>Accessible identity table</summary><p>Same bounded page as the graph. Identity counts and endpoint observation counts are different units.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Canonical identity / select</th><th>First observed UTC</th><th>Last observed UTC</th><th>Source occurrences</th><th>Identity evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody id="topology-table"></tbody></table></div></details>
<section class="panel"><h2>Historical comparison</h2><p>Compare bounded relationship observation sets. The comparison below reports identity observations separately; not re-observed never means disconnected.</p><div class="controls"><label>Baseline start UTC<input type="datetime-local" id="topology-baseline-start" step="1"></label><label>Baseline end UTC<input type="datetime-local" id="topology-baseline-end" step="1"></label><button type="button" id="topology-compare" disabled>Compare windows</button></div><div id="topology-comparison" aria-live="polite"></div></section>
<p>Data sources: historical discovery receipts, usable ENRs and inspection targets. Untimed records and latest-only projections do not become historical observations. Every window is UTC [start, end), at most 31 days. Protocol-specific filters select discovery receipts only. Existing API evidence links preserve source records.</p>
<noscript>This evidence explorer requires JavaScript. Existing authenticated JSON evidence remains available at /api/v1/topology/graph.</noscript></main><script src="/assets/topology.js" defer></script></body></html>
